{"name":"Delays for Pull Requests and Webhook deliveries","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-10-21T14:52:49.979Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T18:41:45.056Z","monitoring_at":null,"resolved_at":"2026-10-21T19:22:52.633Z","impact":"critical","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/gnnt0tx9nxmk","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"critical","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-10-21T14:52:49.969Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"nms1dpzmh9d9","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On October 21, 2026, between 13:22 UTC and 19:22 UTC, several GitHub services were delayed due to degradation of our internal event streaming platform. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003ePull request updates, push webhooks, and push-triggered Actions workflows were delayed by up to 33 minutes until 15:36 UTC. Actions status updates were delayed by up to 33 minutes until 16:16 UTC, holding up some merges and deployments that wait on checks. Webhook deliveries and live updates were delayed by up to 25 minutes until 16:52 UTC. Audit log events were delayed by up to two hours. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was due to servers in the platform running out of memory caused by client reconnections without sufficient retry backoff. We mitigated the incident by moving the busiest workloads to less-loaded servers and adding capacity. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe have since added reconnection backoff and added server capacity. We are building a solution for auto-rebalancing connections across servers, and splitting the platform into smaller, isolated clusters to reduce blast radius and time to mitigation of issues like this one in the future.","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:22:52.633Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-11-16T18:41:45.052Z","display_at":"2026-10-21T19:22:52.633Z","delive